5:Sections: decisions, migrations, jobs, tool surface, journal builder, stops and open risk, snapshots, UI, testing, deploy, build order, deferred items, Schwab assumptions, working method.
30:| 3 | `accounts` | `schwab_hash` (Schwab's opaque hashValue, unique), `account_type` enum (taxable/ira, nullable: set by the operator since Schwab only reports CASH or MARGIN), `trading_enabled` bool, `nickname`, `last_synced_at`, `raw` jsonb. A plaintext account number is never a column. | yes |
31:| 4 | `instruments` | `cusip` (nullable, unique where present), `schwab_instrument_id` (nullable, unique where present), `symbol`, `symbol_history` jsonb `[{symbol, until}]` (UTC), `asset_type`, `leveraged` bool default false, `description`, `predecessor_instrument_id` (self FK, set on CUSIP succession: reverse split, merger, spin-off). Identity resolution order: CUSIP, then Schwab instrument id, then symbol+asset_type as last resort with a `needs_review` audit. | yes |
37:| 10 | `activities` (the PRD's `transactions`; renamed because `transaction` is reserved by Active Record) | One row per Schwab activity. `account_id`, `instrument_id` (nullable for cash-only), `order_id` (FK, nullable), `broker_order_id` (nullable), `broker_activity_id` (unique per account), `kind` enum (fill, dividend, interest, fee, deposit, withdrawal, corporate_action, other), `sub_type` string (raw Schwab type), `side`, `quantity`, `price`, `commission`, `fees` (summed from the activity's fee transfer items), `net_amount`, `trade_date`, `settlement_date`, `executed_at`, `raw` jsonb, `journaled_at` | yes |
62:| `Schwab::RefreshAccessTokenJob` | every 25 min | POST refresh grant; update `schwab_tokens` (`refresh_expires_at` untouched); on failure audit `token_refresh_failed`; no-op when refresh token expired |
63:| `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` | daily 08:00 + 20:00 | Nag when `refresh_expires_at` < now + 24h. Escalation rule: on Monday and Tuesday, email if `refresh_expires_at` is before the coming Sunday 18:00 email plus 12h buffer (Sunday re-auth was missed). Audit each nag. |
80:**Schwab client:** built to `docs/schwab-api-contract.md`. Net::HTTP; plaintext account numbers scrubbed inside the client before any body is returned; logs carry path templates (`/accounts/{hash}/orders`), never hashes, bodies, or headers; one time helper for the three input and three output formats; `BigDecimal` for every money and quantity value; a shared Solid Cache rate budget of 100 requests/minute across Puma and the worker; retries on 429, 5xx, and transport errors for GETs and the refresh grant only (1, 4, 16 s with jitter, `Retry-After` capped at 60 s), never on 4xx; one refresh-and-retry on a 401. Error classes: `AuthError`, `ReauthRequired`, `RateLimited`, `ServerError`, `RequestError`, `TransportError`, `UnknownOutcome` (non-idempotent calls only, chosen by HTTP method), `MappingError`. Interface adds `order(hash, order_id)` so working stops older than the lookback are re-fetched by id, and `instrument(symbol_or_cusip)` for identity fallback. Mappers return `Data` structs with a scrubbed `raw` member; jobs never see a Schwab field name. `Schwab::FakeClient` sits below the mappers and returns raw-shaped hashes with a scriptable per-call queue. Sync runs can finish `partial` with an `unmapped_values` count when individual records are quarantined.
92:| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at; when the token is expired returns the cached value with `stale: true` or an explicit unavailable error |
93:| `get_price_history(symbol, range)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/pricehistory`, cached 5 min |
159:| Re-auth | `/schwab/authorize` → Schwab → `/schwab/callback` | Requires login; success page with new expiry and catch-up sync enqueued; failure page with error and retry |
171:- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
172:- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
191:3. Schwab adapter: `Schwab::Client` (OAuth, accounts, positions, orders, transactions, market hours, quotes, price history) with retry/backoff/limiter, `Schwab::FakeClient`, response mappers, `docs/verify-on-approval.md` started from §12.
